    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d847">

                <pb facs="0783" n="611" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp01v01/pg611"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 124.62/39</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Spain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Willard</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-02-13T22:00:00+00:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 13, 1917, 10 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received February 13, 7 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>350. Foreign Office informs me Spanish Ambassador, Berlin officially took charge
                    American interests February 6, but that owing to presence of American Ambassador
                    and staff he only actually took charge and opened special office for American
                    interests February 12. Spanish Ambassador states that Ambassador Gerard and Grew asked him to employ Vice Consul Von
                        Versen to assist in connection with American interests.
                        Versen is American citizen but German by birth and
                    Spanish Ambassador asks to be informed as soon as possible whether Department
                    would wish him to be employed under the circumstances.<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d847-f1"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Willard</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d847-f1" n="1" xml:id="d847-f1-content">
                <p>Assent to his employment temporarily given in telegram of Feb. 16 (No. 259) to
                    the Ambassador. Same file number; not printed.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
